10. ADVANCED CONTACT PRIVACY SETTINGS
==================================================

Every contact method must have its own independent privacy configuration.

For each contact field, provide three visibility levels:

1. PUBLIC

All users who are authorized to view the profile can see this contact information.

2. MATCHES ONLY

Only users with an active mutual Match can see this information.

3. PRIVATE

Only the account owner can see this information.

Default privacy:

Instagram: Private.
Telegram: Private.
WhatsApp: Private.
Website: Private.
Email: Private.
Mobile phone: Private.

Important privacy requirements:

- Email must be private by default.
- Mobile number must be private by default.
- Every contact method requires separate user approval before becoming visible.
- Every field must be independently editable.
- Users must be able to revoke visibility at any time.
- Users must be able to delete contact information.
- Never show private contacts in search results.
- Never include contact information in discovery cards.
- Never expose contacts in public profile API responses.
- Never include private contacts in matchmaking calculations.
- Never reveal contact details to blocked users.
- Removing a Match must immediately revoke Match-only access.
- Blocking another user must revoke their access.

Store contact information separately from public profile documents.

Suggested Firestore structure:

users/{uid}/private_data/contact_information

Example schema:

{
  instagram: {
    value: "@username",
    visibility: "private",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  },

  telegram: {
    value: "https://t.me/username",
    visibility: "matches",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  },

  whatsapp: {
    value: "+989xxxxxxxxx",
    visibility: "private",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  },

  website: {
    value: "https://example.com",
    visibility: "public",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  },

  email: {
    value: "name@example.com",
    visibility: "private",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  },

  mobile: {
    value: "+989xxxxxxxxx",
    visibility: "private",
    enabled: true,
    updatedAt: "serverTimestamp"
  }
}

Implement server-side access control.

Never rely on frontend-only privacy checks.

Create a secure backend function:

getAuthorizedProfileContacts(profileOwnerUid)

The function must:

1. Authenticate the requesting user.
2. Identify the profile owner.
3. Check whether the requesting user is the owner.
4. Check whether an active mutual Match exists.
5. Check whether either account has blocked the other.
6. Read the individual privacy settings.
7. Return only the fields the requester is authorized to see.
8. Exclude all unauthorized fields.

Do not return the complete contact document and hide fields with CSS.

Only return authorized contact information from the backend.

Validate and sanitize every contact value.

URL security:

- Allow HTTPS links.
- Validate domains and URL formats.
- Reject javascript: URLs.
- Reject data: URLs.
- Reject unsafe redirect destinations.
- Sanitize user input.
- Validate email formats.
- Validate international phone numbers.
- Normalize WhatsApp numbers.
- Validate Telegram usernames and links.
- Validate Instagram usernames and URLs.

